      <div class="modal-body">
        <p>
          This is a set of tools for teaching English (currently only AmE) in
          class or remote lessons.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the
            <img src="/image/students.svg" class="material-icons" alt="Home" style="width:1.4rem;height:1.4rem;">
            button to go to the student friendly version of this site. Have your students bookmark it.
          </li>
          <li>Use the 'G3/G4' tab for vocabulary and various activities to use in 3rd and 4th grade lessons.<br />
            You will also find links to the digital resources for Let's Try 1 and Let's Try 2.
          </li>
          <li>Use the 'G5/G6' tab for vocabulary and various activities to use in 5th and 6th grade lessons.</li>
          <li>
            Use the 'Images' tab to study vocabulary using over 680 free open-source images.
            <ul>
              <li>
                The first column allows you to filter for phonics. Select words
                that start with certain letters or include certain sounds.
              </li>
              <li>
                The second column allows you to select words based on various themes.
              </li>
              <li>
                The list will include the intersection of these two columns.
              </li>
              <li>
                You can then filter for number of letters.
              </li>
              <li>
                Finally, you can edit the list manually to remove words you
                don't want to include. You can also add words but be careful.
                It needs to be a word that there is actually an image for.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </li>

          <li>
            The Nametags tab is a tool that allows you to add a comma-separated
            list of names to be printed on A4 paper to create nametags for students.
          </li>
          <li>
            The LP tab is a tool that allows you to create, save and print your
            own simple easy-to-follow lesson plans.
          </li>
          <li>
            The RT tab is a tool that allows you to create, save, and
            print your own rich text documents.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p> Once you start an activity, you should be able to bookmark it so
          that you can easily return to the same activity with the same
          vocabulary later.
        </p>
